DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
     yyaacccc reports each grammar error with the input line number
     and a description; a fatal error (for example a missing "%%"
     or an unreadable grammar file) stops it immediately, and any
     error at all suppresses generation of the parser tables.
     yyaacccc also writes a count of shift/reduce and reduce/reduce
     conflicts.

NNOOTTEESS
     yyaacccc in this tree always writes yy.ttaabb.hh on every run,
     whether or not -dd was given.

     The compiled-in default for the maximum number of terminal
     symbols is 150 (MMAAXXTTEERRMM in yyaacccc.hh), not 300 as given above
     (the other defaults shown -- 100 non-terminals, 175 produc-
     tions, 300 states, 10 types -- agree with the source).
     Also, an explicit -tteerrmmss value of 160 or more makes yyaacccc
     stop with the fatal error ggeett cciiaarraann ttoo cchhaannggee aalllloocc ffoorr
     llsseettss, since the lookahead bitset is sized for at most 159
     terminal symbols.
